ank":"53rd"}],"birthPlace":"Highland, IL","draftText":"2023: Rd 2, Pk 34 (DET)"},"news":[{"headline":"Fantasy football matchup ranks: Upgrade Jonah Coleman, downgrade Brock Purdy","description":"The most and least favorable matchups in the NFL for this week's games at the four key fantasy positions.","published":"2026-11-18T15:09:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50513739/fantasy-football-rankings-best-worst-matchup-qb-rb-wr-te","type":"Story","byline":"Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football matchup rankings: Upgrade Irving, downgrade Williams","description":"The most and least favorable matchups in the NFL for this week's games at the four key fantasy positions.","published":"2026-10-29T14:38:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50289452/fantasy-football-rankings-best-worst-matchup-qb-rb-wr-te","type":"Story","byline":"Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions' Dan Campbell downplays Sam LaPorta's contract comments","description":"Lions coach Dan Campbell is downplaying comments made by Sam LaPorta about the tight end's displeasure with where contract talks stand with the organization. LaPorta later softened the tone on his comments.","published":"2026-10-23T19:09:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50258967/lions-dan-campbell-downplays-sam-laporta-contract-comments","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sam LaPorta not feeling contract 'love' from Lions ahead of 2027 free agency","description":"Tight end Sam LaPorta, who will be a free agent after the season, expressed some frustration that the Lions are \"not showing the love\" and indicated he would be OK with playing elsewhere in 2027.","published":"2026-10-21T19:22:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50240100/sam-laporta-extension-not-feeling-love-lions","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Knockout league pickups: Trio of Lions among best pickups for Week 7","description":"Tristan H. Cockcroft lists the most common players on eliminated teams and finds how much FAB to spend this week.","published":"2026-10-20T17:46:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50229520/fantasy-football-knockout-waiver-wire-free-agent-pickups-nfl-week-7","type":"Story","byline":"Tristan H. Cockcroft","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"TE Sam LaPorta says extension talks with Lions at 'stalemate'","description":"Lions tight end Sam LaPorta is currently focused on the 2026 season but acknowledged for the first time after Wednesday's practice that he has broken off contract talks on an extension.","published":"2026-10-07T22:50:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50127865/te-sam-laporta-says-extension-talks-lions-stalemate","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Facts vs. Feelings: Should you start Brissett, Tate or Burden in Week 5?","description":"Whether you are 4-0 or 0-4, setting a smart Week 5 lineup starts with sorting the facts from your feelings.","published":"2026-10-08T20:03:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50124472/facts-vs-feelings-fantasy-advice-week-5","type":"Story","byline":"Liz Loza","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: TE Sam LaPorta, Lions break off contract talks","description":"The Lions and star tight end Sam LaPorta have broken off contract talks, sources told NFL Network, after attempting to work out a long-term deal for the first few weeks of the season.","published":"2026-10-04T13:52:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50094193/sources-sam-laporta-lions-break-contract-talks","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Ian Rapoport","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy football sleepers, busts and breakouts for 2026","description":"Which players will surprise, disappoint or make a big jump this fantasy season? Our analysts give their picks.","published":"2026-09-04T16:46:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/page/FFSleepBustBreak26-49030808/fantasy-football-2026-rankings-nfl-sleepers-breakouts-busts","type":"Story","byline":"Fantasy staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lions safeties Branch, Joseph expected to return after PUP stints","description":"Lions starting safeties Brian Branch (Achilles) and Kerby Joseph (knee), who will both miss the first four games of the season, are expected to return at some point, according to GM Brad Holmes","published":"2026-09-02T17:36:04.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49804319/lions-safeties-branch-joseph-pup-list-miss-first-4-games","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eric Woodyard","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Sam LaPorta","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sam_LaPorta","description":"American football player (born 2001)","touched":"2026-11-27T17:30:03Z","intro":"Samuel Joseph LaPorta (born January 12, 2001) is an American professional football tight end for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Iowa Hawkeyes with whom he was named the Big Ten Tight End of the Year in 2022.\nLaPorta was selected by the Lions in the second round of the 2023 NFL draft. As a rookie, he was named second-team All-Pro and voted to the Pro Bowl. He also broke the NFL record for receptions by a rookie tight end (since broken by 2024 rookie Brock Bowers), along with setting Lions franchise records for receptions, receiving yards, and touchdowns by a tight end.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"LaPorta attended Highland High School in Illinois and is of Italian descent. He played wide receiver and defensive back in high school. During his career he had 3,793 receiving yards and 50 touchdowns. LaPorta committed to the University of Iowa to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"2019 SEASON\nLaPorta entered his freshman season in 2019 behind Nate Wieting and Shaun Beyer in the depth chart. In Week 8 against Northwestern, LaPorta caught his first two career passes for 43 yards in a 20–0 win. In 2019, LaPorta played in 12 games with two starts and had 15 receptions for 188 yards.\n\n2020 SEASON\nAs a sophomore in 2020, LaPorta split starting duties with Beyer for the second year in a row. Against Purdue, LaPorta had a career-high 71 receiving yards on five receptions in a 24–20 loss. He caught his first career touchdown against Illinois while having four receptions for 57 yards in a 35–21 win. LaPorta played in eight games with five starts while recording 27 receptions for 271 yards and one touchdown. He was also named Fourth-Team All-Big Ten Conference by Phil Steele and honorable-mention All-Big Ten by the coaches and media.\n\n2021 SEASON\nLaPorta became the starting tight end in 2021. He was placed on the Mackey Award Preseason Watch List and was named Preseason Third-Team All-Big Ten by Athlon Sports and Phil Steele. In their first game against ranked Indiana, LaPorta set a new career-best with 83 yards on five receptions in a 34–6 blowout win. Against Kent State, LaPorta caught a career-best seven catches while totaling 65 yards and adding a touchdown in a 30–7 win. He caught another touchdown against Colorado State in a 24–14 win. Against ranked Kentucky in the 2022 Citrus Bowl, LaPorta had his first 100-yard game with seven receptions, matching a career-high, for 122 yards and a touchdown that gave the Hawkeyes the lead. …"},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"2023 SEASON\nThe Detroit Lions selected LaPorta with the 34th overall pick in the second round of the 2023 NFL draft.\nOn September 24, 2023, LaPorta became the first tight end to tally five receptions in each of his first three games as well as having the most receptions by a tight end in that stretch with 18. He also caught his first career touchdown pass on a 45-yard catch-and-run from Jared Goff. The Lions would end up beating the Atlanta Falcons, 20–6. With his four receptions in Week 4 against the Green Bay Packers, LaPorta broke the record for receptions by a tight end in their first four games with 22. A week later in Week 5 against the Carolina Panthers, LaPorta caught a pair of touchdowns for the first multi-touchdown game of his career while also having three receptions for 47 yards. The Lions would win, 42–24.\nIn Week 8, LaPorta broke the Lions' franchise record for receptions by a rookie tight end with 43, breaking Charlie Sanders' record of 40 that he set in 1968. During the game, he caught eight passes for 57 yards and a touchdown in the 26–14 win over the Las Vegas Raiders. In the Lions'  22–29 loss to the Packers on Thanksgiving, LaPorta broke Sanders' franchise record of 533 yards by a rookie tight end when he had five catches for 47 yards and a touchdown. In Week 13, LaPorta broke the franchise record for receiving yards by a rookie tight end in a single game with 140 yards and a touchdown on nine receptions. The Lions would beat the New Orleans Saints, 33–28. He was named Pepsi NFL Rookie of the Week for his performance.\nIn the Lions' Week 15 win over the Denver Broncos, LaPorta became the first rookie tight end since Jeremy Shockey in 2002 to record 70 receptions in a season while also becoming the first rookie tight end since Joseph Fauria in 2013 to record three receiving touchdowns in a single game. He was recognized again as the Pepsi NFL Rookie of the Week for the second time in three weeks. In Week 18 against the Minnesota Vikings, LaPorta broke the single-season rookie tight end record for receptions with 82. It also came on his 10th touchdown of the season. LaPorta also left the game early after hyperextending his knee. After finishing the season with 86 receptions, 889 yards, and a tight end leading 10 touchdowns, LaPorta was named to the 2024 Pro Bowl Games. He was also selected as a Second-team All-Pro by the Associated Press. LaPorta was also named a finalist for the Pepsi Zero Sugar NFL Rookie of the Year Award.\nLaPorta set many Lions records during his rookie season. He set new records for receptions, receiving yards, and receiving touchdowns by a tight end overall. All of which were also the Lions' rookie tight end records. His 10 receiving touchdowns were also the record for Lions rookies overall. He was an Offensive Rookie of the Year finalist. He was named to the PFWA All-Rookie Team.\nIn his first postseason game, LaPorta scored a receiving touchdown in the Wild Card Round win over the Rams. He was ranked 80th by his fellow players on the NFL Top 100 Players of 2024.\n\n2024 SEASON\nIn the 2024 season, LaPorta finished with 60 receptions for 726 yards and seven touchdowns. He scored a receiving touchdown in the Lions' Divisional Round loss to the Washington Commanders. While his production dropped from his first season, LaPorta nonetheless joined Mike Ditka, Rob Gronkowski, and Jimmy Graham as only the fourth tight end in NFL history to log 1,500 receiving yards and 15 receiving touchdowns in his first two seasons. He was ranked 94th by his fellow players on the NFL Top 100 Players of 2025.\n\n2025 SEASON\nLaPorta began the 2025 season as Detroit's starting tight end, and recorded 489 yards and three touchdowns over the team's first nine games. After suffering a back injury in Week 10 against the Washington Commanders, LaPorta was placed on injured reserve on November 15, 2025. On November 21, it was announced that LaPorta was unlikely to return during the season after undergoing back surgery. He finished 40 receptions for 489 yards and three touchdowns."},{"key":"awards","title":"Career highlights","text":"AWARDS AND HONORS\nNFL\n\nSecond-team All-Pro (2023)\nPro Bowl (2023)\nPFWA All-Rookie Team (2023)\n2× NFL Top 100 — 80th (2024), 94th (2025)\nCollege\n\nBig Ten Tight End of the Year (2022)\nFirst-team All-Big Ten (2022)\nSecond-team All-Big Ten (2021)\nHonorable mention All-Big Ten – Coaches and Media (2020)\nPhil Steele fourth-team All-American (2022)\n\nRECORDS\n\nNFL RECORDS\nTied for most touchdowns by a rookie tight end in the Super Bowl era\n\nLIONS FRANCHISE RECORDS\nMost receptions by a tight end in a single season: 86 (2023)\nMost receptions by a tight end in a rookie season: 86 (2023)\nMost receiving yards by a tight end in a single season: 889 (2023)\nMost receiving yards by a tight end in a rookie season: 889 (2023)\nMost receiving touchdowns by a tight end in a single season: 10 (2023)\nMost receiving touchdowns by a tight end in a rookie season: 10 (2023)\nMost receiving touchdowns by a player in a rookie season: 10 (2023)\nMost receiving yards by a tight end in a rookie game: 140 (December 3, 2023, vs. New Orleans Saints)"}],"wikidataId":"Q108830207","social":{"x":"Samlaporta","instagram":"_slaporta"}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430027","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/L/LaPoSa01.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/sam-laporta/101690","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/sam-laporta/10858","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sam_LaPorta"},"insights":["Ranks 3rd of 43 qualified tight ends in receiving epa.","Ranks 1st of 43 qualified tight ends in drop %.","On the field for 75% of Detroit’s offensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $6.7M is the 10th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}